										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><a href="https://www.mysaline.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Celebrate-Lamar-1400-x-400-px-840-x-400-px_20240724_074016_0000.png"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="aligncenter wp-image-100442 size-medium" src="https://www.mysaline.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Celebrate-Lamar-1400-x-400-px-840-x-400-px_20240724_074016_0000-300x240.png" alt="" width="300" height="240" srcset="https://www.mysaline.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Celebrate-Lamar-1400-x-400-px-840-x-400-px_20240724_074016_0000-300x240.png 300w, https://www.mysaline.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Celebrate-Lamar-1400-x-400-px-840-x-400-px_20240724_074016_0000-150x120.png 150w, https://www.mysaline.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Celebrate-Lamar-1400-x-400-px-840-x-400-px_20240724_074016_0000.png 600w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px" /></a></p>
<p>Organizers of Downtown Benton&#8217;s Third Thursday have announced the cancellation of their upcoming August 20, 2026, event due to a prolonged forecast of intense heat. With triple-digit temperatures and dangerous heat indexes expected over the next ten-plus days, officials stated the difficult decision was made to ensure the safety of the community. Read more below.</p>
<hr />
<p><script async src="https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com/pagead/js/adsbygoogle.js?client=ca-pub-9318701447515491" crossorigin="anonymous"></script><br />
