<ins class="adsbygoogle" style="display: block;" data-ad-client="ca-pub-9318701447515491" data-ad-slot="1423088530" data-ad-format="auto" data-full-width-responsive="true"></ins><br />
<script>
     (adsbygoogle = window.adsbygoogle || []).push({});
</script></p>
<hr />
<p>In a public statement, event organizers explained that keeping vendors, food truck operators, musical bands, and local citizens safe is their top priority. The excessive temperatures and high heat indexes made canceling the outdoor summer celebration a necessary precaution to prevent heat-related illnesses among attendees and workers.</p>
<p>While the August festivities are canceled, the popular downtown festival will resume next month. Organizers confirmed the community gathering will return in September for its scheduled &#8220;Faith and Family&#8221; night, and they urge everyone to stay safe and cool in the meantime.</p>
